# News feed: newest first

`index.html` `.recent-news-list` is one reverse-chronological list. Sort by each card’s `<time datetime>`. Newest at the top. Local Crossville cards compete in that same list. Hometown does not jump the date.

## Do

- Insert a new card by its story date, not at the top by default
- Let a Sept. 6 national update sit above a Sept. 2 Crossville card
- Same calendar day: keep existing same-day order; do not invent a local-first tie-break

## Do not

- Pin Crossville / `data-geo="local"` above a later-dated card
- Treat “most important locally” as a reason to break date order
- Re-date an old card to make it look newer (`recent-news-story-updates.mdc`)

```html
<!-- BAD: Sept. 2 local above Sept. 6 national -->
<li data-geo="local">… <time datetime="2026-09-02">…</time></li>
<li data-geo="national">… <time datetime="2026-09-06">…</time></li>

<!-- GOOD: date order, local in its slot -->
<li data-geo="national">… <time datetime="2026-09-06">…</time></li>
<li data-geo="local">… <time datetime="2026-09-02">…</time></li>
```
